fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0245769Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0255946Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0356822Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0366312Z ^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0367014Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0367743Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0368108Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0368509Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0370057Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0370783Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0371143Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0371883Z    if you are ready to continue.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0372233Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0372890Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0374144Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0375076Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0375750Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0376066Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0376468Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0376980Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0377372Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0378089Z    can use Nix.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0378329Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0378459Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0378670Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0379018Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0379957Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0380392Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0380579Z I will:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0380889Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0381242Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0381999Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0382775Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0383946Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0384495Z  - install Nix in /nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0385009Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0385772Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0386210Z    /root
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0394707Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0395646Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0405726Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0406516Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0406808Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0407609Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0408261Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0425494Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0426080Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0436767Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0437525Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0438329Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0438721Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0439054Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0439513Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0439884Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0440940Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0441531Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0441676Z If you would like to
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0441976Z see the output, try like this:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0442175Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0442386Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-13T09:44:00.0442815Z   $ sh ./install-nix
